1
00:00:01,299 --> 00:00:04,519
For the demo, let's log into our Google Cloud console.

2
00:00:04,739 --> 00:00:07,139
Here, I'm inside the Google Cloud console.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,050
I'm logged in as an organizational admin,

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:13,939
which gives me the permission to create the folders and

5
00:00:13,939 --> 00:00:15,800
projects at the organizational level.

6
00:00:15,899 --> 00:00:19,180
You can access this by navigating here.

7
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:23,159
Go to the IAM and admin and click on Manage resources.

8
00:00:24,299 --> 00:00:28,299
This page is the tree view of your entire cloud footprint.

9
00:00:28,459 --> 00:00:33,200
If your organization is brand new, you probably see only one thing,

10
00:00:33,299 --> 00:00:36,700
your organization name, with generally your company name.

11
00:00:36,819 --> 00:00:37,659
That's perfect.

12
00:00:37,779 --> 00:00:38,990
But in my case,

13
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:44,360
I've already created a couple of projects and folders inside this organization.

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,779
That's why you are seeing a couple of them.

15
00:00:46,939 --> 00:00:50,069
Let me just create one new folder.

16
00:00:50,259 --> 00:00:52,939
So on the top here you see Create folder.

17
00:00:53,639 --> 00:00:58,220
Let me create a folder, name as production and say Create.

18
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,500
Whenever you create the folder, internally,

19
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,160
Google assigns it a numeric ID corresponding to it.

20
00:01:05,279 --> 00:01:09,620
For example, right now we are not able to see the folder that we have created.

21
00:01:10,099 --> 00:01:13,839
Just click on Refresh so that it will be visible here.

22
00:01:14,019 --> 00:01:17,580
Now you can see that I have a production folder, and I

23
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:19,739
can see a corresponding numerical ID.

24
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:24,800
We can think about creating multiple folders corresponding to environment.

25
00:01:25,019 --> 00:01:29,379
For example, I can create one more folder for staging.

26
00:01:30,349 --> 00:01:34,400
And similarly, I create one more folder for the development,

27
00:01:34,489 --> 00:01:38,160
so I click on here, say Folder, and say development.

28
00:01:39,239 --> 00:01:41,099
Now if I refresh it again,

29
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:46,180
I can see all those folder that I've already created, development,

30
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,620
staging, and production.

31
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:53,220
Now it's time to go ahead and populate these folders with application projects.

32
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:57,779
You might have multiple applications, maybe like payment service,

33
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,720
inventory service, or a notification service.

34
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:04,279
What you can think about is having all those

35
00:02:04,279 --> 00:02:06,730
applications in each of these environments.

36
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:11,669
For example, let's click on Create project, and let's say create a project,

37
00:02:11,869 --> 00:02:14,350
say, payment‑app‑service‑prod.

38
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:19,550
Now what I will do is I click on Browse here because I want this

39
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:23,669
project to get created within my development folder.

40
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,729
So I select the development and say Create.

41
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:33,869
Now you will see that under the Notifications, a project has started initiating.

42
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:34,220
Now,

43
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:38,240
if I simply refresh and if I expand this development

44
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:42,919
tab, you can see a project inside it.

45
00:02:43,279 --> 00:02:47,720
Now what I can do is, when I move to the staging or I move to the production,

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:48,610
similarly,

47
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:51,880
I will create this kind of project into my staging

48
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,279
folder and in my production folder.

49
00:02:54,949 --> 00:02:56,580
Maybe I have multiple applications.

50
00:02:57,270 --> 00:03:01,229
So correspondingly, I can create multiple projects

51
00:03:01,229 --> 00:03:02,800
within a single folder itself.

52
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,100
So if you look at it,

53
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:08,199
we have created the entire hierarchy for our

54
00:03:08,199 --> 00:03:10,960
project, which involves development, staging,

55
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:14,979
and the production. And we have not talked about the IAM yet,

56
00:03:15,279 --> 00:03:17,860
but the moment you create a folder,

57
00:03:18,119 --> 00:03:21,410
a couple of roles have been assigned to these folders.

58
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:25,399
You can go down to the settings, and you can click on the IAM here

59
00:03:25,399 --> 00:03:29,740
and you can see that, a couple of roles and permissions have been

60
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:32,940
assigned to this specific folder.
